      "description": "Faculty | Mission University Search for: REQUEST ADMISSIONS INFORMATION VISIT CAMPUS LOGINS GIVE APPLY About About Accreditation Beliefs & Values Consumer Information Contact Institutional Learning Outcomes Institutional Research & Effectiveness Hours of Operation Leadership Admissions Admissions Connect With Us Request Info Visit Campus Student Housing Tuition & Fees Tuition and Fees 2026-27 Financial Aid Transfer to Mission U Academics Academics Academic Calendar Dual Credit / Dual Enrollment On-Campus Degrees Online Degrees Faculty Library Transcript Request Diploma Request Graduation Campus Events Campus Events Calendar Patriot Days Student Life Campus Events Calendar Chapel & Community Groups Dining Services 26-27 Student Housing Athletics Apparel Alumni & Friends Resources Book MU Worship Campus Mail Campus Security Consumer Information EADA Report Job Opportunities News Professional Licensure Disclosure Resources Student Login Faculty MISSION STATEMENT Mission University educates, inspires, and equips students to serve as effective Christian leaders. RAY ADAMS Bible History Faculty – 1979 Education: BA, Mission University, 1977; MA History, Southwest Missouri State University, 1980; MA Religious Studies, Southwest Missouri State University, 1996. Local Church: Cherry Street Baptist (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Philippians 2:1-5 Hobbies: Fishing, racquetball, leading tours to Israel, and Pickleball Publications: “A Zealot’s Redemption,” Critical Mass Books, 2021; “A Zealot’s Reconciliation,” Tribune Publishing, 2024 Bio: Dr. Adams has worked at Mission University for over 45 years. He served as the Dean of Students during the administration of three MU presidents over the course of 25 years. For the last few years, Dr. Adams has been a full-time faculty member, teaching courses like Life of Christ, Old Testament Survey, History of Western Civilization, Church History, and History of Baptists. Dr. Adams says that it has been his joy to teach thousands of students over his tenure as the longest-serving faculty member in Mission University history, and this may be why he is the first person to teach History classes. CARLTON AMES Online Degrees Faculty; Business & Leadership – 2024 Education: BA, Judson University, 1985; MBA, National Louis University, 2002; Ed.D. Organizational Leadership, Nova Southeastern University, 2007. MARK BALLMER Online Degrees Faculty; Bible & Theology – 2009 Education: BS, Mission University, 2004; M.Div., Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2009; D.Min., Ashland Theological Seminary, 2013. Local Church: Westwood Baptist (OH) Favorite Bible Passage: 1 Corinthians 15:58 Hobbies: Reading, sprots, traveling Bio: Dr. Ballmer started full-time in ministry in 1980 and has served at Westwood Baptist Church in Zanesville, OH since 1986. PHILIP BASSHAM Online Degrees Faculty; Ministry & Leadership – 2021 Education: BA, Mission University, 2004; M.Div., Liberty University, 2010; M.Div.PM, Liberty University, 2013; D.Min. Leadership, Liberty University, 2019. Local Church: Discovery Church Favorite Bible Passage: Joshua 1:9 Hobbies: Auto mechanics, woodworking, home remodeling Publications: “Cultural Kingdom Architects: Defining Success in Building God’s Kingdom” Bio: Vocational ministry leadership has always been of interest to Dr. Bassham, particularly the pieces that make ministry flow and function. Beginning with Pastoral Theology at Mission University in the early 2000’s and continuing into pastoral ministry, Dr. Bassham has had a desire to invest in the men and women entering ministry so that they can be more prepared for what they will face in their ministries. This is why he chooses to be a part of the faculty of Mission U. CHRISTOPHER BECK Director of Online Education; Chair of Online Education; General Studies Faculty – 1991 Education: BA, Mission University, 1984; MA Communication, Southwest Missouri State University, 1992; Ph.D. Communication, Regent University, 2004. Local Church: West Republic Baptist (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: 1 Samuel 12:24 Hobbies: Performing as a magician, creating original magical illusions, singing, and writing songs Website: westrepublicbaptist.com Publications: – “4 Reasons to Choose a Christian College.” Christian Academia Magazine (October 2017) – “Magic Moments” (Newsletter for Performing Artists who are IBM Ring #325 members) Newsletter – Founding editor/writer, monthly publication (April 2015-Present) – “When the President Invited God to the Inauguration.” Baptist Bible Tribune/BBFI (Issue 6, Volume 59) (2009) – “Presidential Inaugurals: A Quantitative Analysis of First and Second American Presidential Inaugural Addresses as Subsets Within the Rhetorical Context.” Regent University (2004) – TheLink (editor) Institutional Newsletter. Baptist Bible College (2002) Professional Affiliations: Central States Communication Association, Religions Communication Association, International Brotherhood of Magicians (IBM) Bio: Dr. Christopher Beck is married to his best friend, Dana. Their son Lincoln awaits them in Heaven. Dr. Beck is the son of Mr. and Mrs. Raymond Beck. (Dr. Beck’s mother, Marilyn Anita Beck, recently made her journey to Heaven, as well). Upon graduation from Mission University, Dr. Gillming, Sr. Reached out to Beck, inviting him to work with Missouri Moral Majority. Opportunities in this position included hosting a weekly radio broadcast and attending a White House briefing with then-President Ronald Reagan). Beck has also worked with the White House Press Advance Team for various presidential events. Beck’s work at MU began at radio station KWFC. Beck earned his master’s degree at MSU and his Ph.D. from Regent University. Dr. Beck is Academic Chair of Online Education at Mission University, pastor of West Republic Baptist Church, and a Chaplain for the Republic Missouri Police Department. He also serves as BBFI (Baptist Bible Fellowship International) field representative for the countries of Italy, Belgium, Slovakia, Croatia and Ukraine. Dr. Beck uses illusions to share the Gospel. He is a member of the International Brotherhood of Magicians (IBM) and has served as President of Branson’s IBM Ring #325. DANA BECK Education Faculty – 2019 Education: BS, Southwest Baptist University, 1989; M.Ed. Elementary Education, Southwest Missouri State University, 1996. Local Church: West Republic Baptist (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Matthew 6:33, John 14:6 Professional Affiliations: Missouri State Teachers Association, Missouri Retired Teachers Association, and National Association for the Education of Young Children Bio: Dana is an adjunct professor at Mission University where she primarily teaches in the Education Department. She is married to Dr. Christopher Beck who also teaches at MU. After their son, Lincoln, passed away, Dana got involved in Good News Club (GNC). GNC is an after-school Bible Club that meets in an area public school. Since 2009, their church has sponsored three clubs where they have been blessed to many young students put their faith in Jesus Christ to be their Savior. While the Becks do not have any living children, their desire is to invest in the lives of the students at GNC and at Mission U. JULIE A. BECK Chair of Professional Studies; Business Department Head; Business Faculty – 1986 Education: BS, Mission University, 1983; M.Ed., Drury College, 1992. Local Church: Second Baptist (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Proverbs 3:5-6 Hobbies: Spending time with family, Nebraska football (Go Big Red!), rescue dogs, gardening Professional Affiliations: NBEA Bio: Julie was raised in a loving, Christian home and attended church whenever the doors were open. She even attended a Christian school. However, she did not know Jesus as her Lord and Savior until she was in the sixth grade when her mother led her to the Lord. From that point on, she has never doubted her salvation. She is a proud graduate of Baptist Bible College (now Mission U.). She enjoys the personal contact with students and desires to improve and enhance their learning experiences. She says our university impacts the world by developing future Christian leaders and that it is so rewarding to be part of that mission. She says she cannot begin to describe what this school has meant to her over the years and that it is a joy for her to have the privilege of teaching at Mission University. She doesn’t take it lightly. She prays that she will make a difference in students’ lives inside and outside the classroom. CLINTON W. BERGMAN Online Degrees Faculty; Old Testament & Hebrew – 2016 Education: BA, Texas A&M University, 2000; MAIS, Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2006; M.Div., Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2008; Ph.D. Old Testament, Clark Summit University, 2017. Local Church: Life Point Church (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: The book of Job Hobbies: Coaching his kids’ sports teams, privately training his kids and their friends in baseball, volleyball, and football as well as personal conditioning, playing games with family and friends, spending time with neighbors. Publications: “Checkers with My Daughter: Life Coaching Through Games” Bio: Dr. Bergman is a former full-time, Old Testament and Hebrew seminary professor. He now teaching online classes in the Baptist Bible Theological Seminary. He is also a full-time business owner. DAVID BOTTS Church Ministry: Family Concentration Department Head; Bible & Theology Faculty – 2015 Education: BA, Mission University, 2012; MABS, Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2015; M.Div., Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2016; Ph.D. Systematic Theology, Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary, ABD. Local Church: Crossway Baptist Church (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: 1 Timothy 4:16 Hobbies: Golf, reading books, watching all things Iowa Hawkeyes Website: bookswithbotts.com Bio: David has served in some teaching role at Mission University since 2012. He is responsible for teaching all theology classes at Mission U and has a desire to see students see how theology affects their everyday lives. In addition to teaching theology, David serves as the department chair for the Church Ministries: Family Concentration degree. He loves helping students discover how to serve effectively in the local church as a staff member or staff pastor. JESSICA BOTTS Education Department Head; Education Faculty – 2024 Education: BS, Mission University, 2012; M.Ed. Educational Leadership, Evangel University, 2020. Local Church: Crossway Baptist (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Jeremiah 29:11 Hobbies: Thrifting and antiquing, reading, spending time with her husband and two kids Bio: Jessica serves as the head of the Education Department at Mission University. In this position, she says she has the opportunity to continually help improve how we prepare future educators to go out from MU and not only excellent teachers, but also godly influences in the teaching profession. She loves being in the classroom where she can speak into student’s lives as they are trained in the profession of teaching. MARK BRAUNBERGER Sciences Faculty – 2023 Education: BS, Evangel University, 2018; DPT, Missouri State University, 2021; Certified Athletic Trainer (ATC); Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist (CSCS). TERRY LEE BROWN Online Degrees Faculty; Business – 2021 Education: BS, Mission University, 1976; MBA, University of Phoenix, 2005. Local Church: Maness Memorial Baptist (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Isaiah 26: 3-4; Revelation 20:10 Hobbies: Reading Ralph Compton western books, watching shows like NCIS and Monk, following the Cardinals baseball team and the Arizona Cardinals, radio advertisements and political activism for the conservative causes. Bio: Served on faculty for Christian Schools of Springfield from 1977-1982. Evangelism ministry 1975-1985. Planted a church in Pittsburg, Kansas in 1978. Served at KWFC radio station from 1975-1985. Served with Wal-Mart store management from 1985-1997. Store manager in Carlyle & Salem, Illinois and Houston, Missouri. Owner and general manager for Beth-Eden Bible Camp 2010-2019 (where he grew up). Serving as lead pastor at Maness Memorial Baptist Church in Cabool, Missouri from 2006-Present. Serving in the loan department at Peoples Community Bank in Cabool for 24 years. MATTHEW BURROWS Online Degrees Faculty; Education – 2024 Education: BS, Mission University, 1997; M.Ed., Wilmington University, 2002; Ed.D. Educational Leadership, Wilmington University, 2017. JEREMIAH CATLIN Online Degrees Faculty; Business – 2024 Education: BA, Mission University, 2002; M.Div., Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2005; MBA, Syracuse University, 2018; MPA, Syracuse University, 2018; D.Min., Erskine Theological Seminary, ABD. Local Church: BACH Army Chapel (KY) Favorite Bible Passage: Philippians 4:6-7 Hobbies: Hunting, fishing, taxidermy, bowling, reading, Chess Website: decisionpointeoutdoors.com Bio: Jeremiah has been married to his wife, Shari, since 1996 and they are blessed with two daughters, Hannah and Naomi. He has served as a missionary representative of the BBFI to the military as a US Army Chaplain since 2005. He is the president and founder of Chappy’s Outdoors non-profit organization ministering to over 1500 wounded veterans. He is the host and producer of the nationwide hunting television show and ministry, Decision Pointe Outdoors. CRAIG CARSON Online Degrees Faculty; Education – 2024 Education: BS, Mission University, 1994; BA, Mission University, 1995; MS Secondary Education, Missouri State University, 2001; Ed.S. Educational Leadership, Saint Louis University, 2006; Ed.D. Educational Leadership, Saint Louis University, 2013. KEVIN CARSON Biblical Counseling Department Head; Biblical Counseling Faculty – 1999 Education: BS, Mission University, 1994; BA, Mission University, 1995; MABS, Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 1996; M.Div., Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 1997; D.Min. Pastoral Counseling, Westminster Theological Seminary, 2004; Certified Biblical Counselor, ACBC. Local Church: Sonrise Baptist (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: 2 Corinthians 5:9 Hobbies: Spending time with family, sports, fishing, hunting, and writing Website: kevincarson.com Publications: Contributor (“Living Today with Tomorrow in Mind”), Randy Harp editor, Higher Ground: Lessons from the Greatest Sermon Every Preached (Tribune Publishers, 2023) “When Brothers Dwell in Unity,” Baptist Bible Tribune (January 2023) “A Christian Who Golfs or a Golfer Who Is a Christian?” Baptist Bible Tribune (April 2022) “In Memory of Dr. Leland Kennedy,” Baptist Bible Tribune (July 2021) “The Most Important Question to Ask at Summer Camp,” Baptist Bible Tribune (July 2021) Contributor (Chapter 11, “Talking with Children about Sex”), Amy Baker editor, Caring for the Souls of Children: A Biblical Counselor’s Manuel (New Growth Press, 2020) Contributor (“Why Is This Decision so Hard to Make?” Proverbs 17), Randy Harp editor, Searching for Wisdom: a 31-day Devotional (Tribune Publishers, 2020) Contributor, “The Right Angle,” Baptist Bible Tribune (-2019) “A Tribute to Ken Howard,” Baptist Bible Tribune (December 2018) “Pastors and Suicide: What Pastors and Congregations Need to Know,” Baptist Bible Tribune (September 2018) “Dear God and Parents, Help Our Children,” Baptist Bible Tribune (March 2018) “Sin: Hope and Help in Christ,” Baptist Bible Tribune (March 2017) “Before You Counsel a Same-Sex Couple,” Baptist Bible Tribune (October 2015) Managing Editor and Contributor, Bob Kellemen and Kevin Carson editors, Biblical Counseling and the Church (Zondervan, 2015) “A Pastoral Response to a Tragedy,” Baptist Bible Tribune (March 2014) “Do You Love Your Community?” Baptist Bible Tribune (August 2014) Contributor (Chapter 1, “The Richness and Relevance of God’s Word”), Bob Kellemen and Jeff Forrey editors, Scripture and Counseling (Zondervan, 2014) “Perspective,” Baptist Bible Tribune (November 2013) Contributor (Chapter 4, “The Unity of the Trinity” with Jeff Forrey and Chapter 17, “The Personal, Private, and Pulpit Ministry of the Word”), Bob Kellemen, and Steve Viars editors, Christ-Centered Biblical Counseling (Harvest House, 2013) “Celebrating Jesus This Christmas,” Baptist Bible Tribune (December 2012) “AfterWords: Windows of Thanksgiving,” Baptist Bible Tribune (November 2012) Contributor (Chapter 9, “Homosexuality”), Stuart Scott and Heath Lambert editors, Counseling the Hard Cases (B&H Academic, 2012) “AfterWords: Giving Thanks with Contentment,” Baptist Bible Tribune (November 2010) “Being A Wise Gift-Giver: Choosing the Best Gifts for Everyone on Your Christmas List,” Baptist Bible Tribune (December 2009) “Going with the Flow: How A Busy Life Can Mask Dangerous Temptations,” Baptist Bible Tribune (October 2009) “Personal Ministry Outside the Walls” part 2, Baptist Bible Tribune (October 2007) “Personal Ministry Outside the Walls” part 1, Baptist Bible Tribune (September 2007) “From the Mountaintop Through the Valley,” Baptist Bible Tribune (June 2007) “Hey Parents, Camp’s Over. Now What?” Baptist Bible Tribune (July/August 2006) “Crisis Management for the Believer” Baptist Bible Tribune (October 2005) “Planning to Heal the Breach” The Baptist Preacher’s Journal (Fall 2005) D.Min. Dissertation, Westminster Theological Seminary, “The Well-Planted Church: Vertically Integrated and Horizontally Mutual” (2004) M.Div. Thesis, Baptist Bible Graduate School, “Non-Conflicting Absolutism: An Evaluation of Norman Geisler” (1997) Professional Affiliations: Association of Certified Biblical Counselors Level II Certification, Council Member with Biblical Counseling Coalition, International Association of Biblical Counselors, Board Member Association of Biblical Counselors, Delta Epsilon Chi Bio: Kevin Carson serves as the department chair of biblical counseling at Mission University. He also serves as the Pastor of the Sonrise Baptist Church in Ozark, Missouri. It was his joy to lead a church planting team to all move to Ozark and start this new church in 2002. Since then, the team has changed some, but God has granted him and his family the privilege of serving together at Sonrise. As a pastor, Kevin has served the Baptist Bible Fellowship International (BBFI) as a missions field representative and the Vice President of Education. In addition to his pastoral ministry, he also serves as a counselor at Sonrise Biblical Counseling Ministry, is ACBC Certified, IABC Certified, a council member of the Biblical Counseling Coalition since its inception, author, and is a frequent speaker at conferences, retreats and seminars. Kevin met his wife Kelly here at Mission University. God has blessed them with five children, four who live local and one in heaven. In addition, God has expanded the family with a son-in-law and a grandson. CLINTON CHILES Online Degrees Faculty; Biblical Studies & Church Ministry – 2021 Education: BS, Mission University, 2007; MACM, Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2013; M.Div., Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2018. Local Church: Grace Bible Fellowship (NE) Favorite Bible Passage: 1 John 2:1-2 Hobbies: Spending time with his family, cheering on the Iowa Hawkeyes, reading and watching sports on television Website: gracebiblecentral.com Bio: Clint has been in pastoral ministry for almost two decades. He is passionate about verse-by-verse expositional preaching, theology, and gospel clarity. Clint enjoys helping students nuance their doctrinal positions in the areas of Christology and Pneumatology while helping them understand biblical ecclesiology. TOMMY DYE Sciences Faculty – 2010 Education: BA, Mission University, 1989; M.Ed. Secondary Teaching, Evangel University, 2013; MS Biology, Grand Canyon University, 2024. JOSH ERISMAN Church Ministry: Music & Worship Department Head; Music Faculty – 2012 Education: BS, Missouri State University, 2008; MACM, Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary, 2011; D.Ed.Min. Worship Ministry, Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary, 2024. Local Church: First Baptist of Strafford (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Ephesians 2:1-10 Hobbies: Politics, U.S. Supreme Court, meteorology, parliamentary procedure, reading, and cheering on the Kansas City Chiefs Publications: “The Easel: Magnifying Christ through the Three-Legged Worship Choir Ministry of First Baptist Church of Strafford, Missouri” (D.Ed.Min. diss., Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary, 2024). Professional Affiliations: Member, Missouri Music Men, 2011-Present (served as president in 2018); Member, Greene County Baptist Association Executive Board, 2022-Present; Member, Southern Baptist Church Music Conference, 2022-Present Bio: Dr. Erisman serves as professor of Music & Worship and is the head of the Church Ministry: Worship Department at Mission University, where he has taught since 2012. In addition to his duties at Mission U, Josh has served as Minister of Music & Education at First Baptist Church of Strafford since 2011. He and his wife, Brittany, are the proud parents of Malachi, Lydia, and Josiah. JUAN ESPERRA, JR. History Faculty – 2023 Education: BS, Florida State University, 1996; BS, University of South Florida, 1999; ME, National Louis University, 2004; Graduate Certificate in Ancient and Classical History, American Public University, 2010. Favorite Bible Passage: Psalm 23 Hobbies: Collecting coins and college and professional sports cards and memorabilia, traveling, watching movies, walking the dogs. Publications: “A Social Studies Curriculum that Works,” master’s thesis, National Louis University Bio: Originally from Sarasota, FL, Juan now calls Warner Robins, GA, home. He has been happily married to his high school sweetheart for 11 years, and their shared journey has been a testament to love and partnership. He is a childhood friend of Dean Mulford, and they have always valued deep connections. Juan’s faith has been a cornerstone of his life since he accepted Christ in elementary school, guiding his values and choices. History captivates him, both as a profession and a passion. He finds inspiration in the truth of Sunday School stories and the adventurous spirit of Indiana Jones films. This love for history fuels his curiosity and desire to uncover the past. At home, he shares his life with two beloved dogs, Maggie and Marley, who bring joy and laughter to his days. He is also a sports enthusiast, enjoying both college and professional games, and he loves to travel, seeking new experiences and cultures. Juan says that each journey, whether on the field or across the globe, enriches his life and broadens his perspective, making every moment an opportunity for discovery and growth. Cristina Espinoza-Alguera Online Degrees Faculty; Business & Economics – 2021 Education: Ph.D. in Agricultural Economics, Texas A&M University M.S. in Agricultural Economics, Kansas State University B.A. in Mathematics, University of California Berkeley CYNTHIA EVANS Online Degrees Faculty; Education – 2019 Education: BS, Mission University, 1983; M.Ed. Elementary Secondary Special Reading, Drury University, 1994; Ed.D. Higher Education, University of North Texas, 2001. James Flora Education Faculty – 2025 Education: Southwest Baptist University, Educational Doctorate in Educational Leadership, 2024 Southwest Baptist University, Educational Specialist in Educational Administration, 2023 Arkansas State University, Master of Science in Educational Leadership, 2014 Montana State University, Master of Science in Science Education, 2007 Southwest Baptist University, Bachelor of Science in Chemistry, 2001 Local Church: Crossway Baptist Church (Springfield, MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Philippians 2:5-8 Hobbies: Fishing and Hunting Blog/Website: https://www.crosswaychristianacademy.com/blog Bio: Dr. Jim Flora graduated from Southwest Baptist University with a Bachelors degree in Chemistry in 2001 and began his career in education that same year. Dr. Flora’s education experience includes teaching at the high school and college level, coaching at the high school and college level, and being a high school principal. He currently is the Head of School of Crossway Christian Academy in Springfield, Mo. Along with his bachelor’s degree in Chemistry, Dr. Flora holds Master degrees in Science Education and Educational Leadership, a Specialist degree in Educational Leadership, and a Doctorate in Educational Leadership. Dr. Flora enjoys spending time with family and serving God as a member of Crossway Baptist Church. His passion is helping others grown in their faith by  impacting their Biblical Worldview through sound Biblical teaching. He desires to help Mission University students grow in their faith to best utilize their gifts to glorify God. KYLE GANGEL Biblical Counseling Faculty – 2011 Education: BA, Mission University, 2008; MABC, Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2012; M.Div., Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2012. Local Church: Southern Hills Bible Church (SD) Favorite Bible Passage: 2 Corinthians 5:21 Hobbies: Spending time with family, hiking, fly fishing, and cheering on the Colorado Buffaloes football & basketball teams. Website: gospelmercies.com Publications: “The ‘Dysregulated’ Nervous System: A Biblical Evaluation of Polyvagal Theory.” The Biblical Evaluation Booklet Series (ACBC: Kansas City, 2024) Professional Affiliations: Association of Certified Biblical Counselors (ACBC) Bio: Kyle has served in several ministry contexts including student ministry, discipleship, and biblical counseling. He currently serves as the lead pastor of Southern Hills Bible Church. He resides with his wife Elisabeth and their four boys Custer, SD. Kyle enjoys having a part in the training of the next generation of pastors, missionaries, Christian leaders, and Biblical counselors as part of the faculty of Mission University. BRUCE GARNER Online Degrees Faculty; Preaching & Teaching – 2021 Education: BA, Pacific Coast Baptist Bible College, 1992; M.Div., Biola University, 1996; D.Min. Theology: Ministry Skills, Biola University, 2020. Local Church: CrossPoint (CA) Favorite Bible Passage: 2 Corinthians 4:5 Hobbies: Reading of all kinds, rucking, and finding great Mexican food all over America Website: crosspointb.org Publications: “The Resilient Pastor: How to Remain Effective and Finish Well in Ministry.” ChurchSmart Resources, 2021. Bio: Born in Amarillo, Texas, but raised in Chihuahua, Mexico, Bruce is a third-generation minister in the Baptist Bible Fellowship. He served with his family as a missionary in Mexico before becoming the senior pastor of his sending church, CrossPoint Church in Huntington Beach, California in 2005. He holds an M.Div (Missions) and a Doctor of Ministry from Biola University. His dissertation led to the publication of the book, “The Resilient Pastor: How to Remain Effective and Finish Well in Ministry.” Bruce has also volunteered as a police chaplain since 2014 and has a personal and academic interest in how people in challenging vocations can remain effective and resilient for life. BRIAN GARRISON Missions/Intercultural Studies Faculty – 2021 Education: BS, Mission University, 1994; MACCM, Dallas Theological Seminary, 1997. Local Church: Park Crest Baptist (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: 1 John 4:4 Hobbies: Golf, church softball Professional Affiliations: Baptist Bible Fellowship International Bio: Brian is a 1994 graduate of Mission University, where he met his wife Mychelle. After earning a master’s degree at Dallas Theological Seminary in 1997, Brian and Mychelle began an internship at First Baptist Church in Vilonia, Arkansas. The Garrisons were approved as BBFI missionaries to Peru in September 2001. They began serving God in Peru in April 2003 and enjoyed a very fruitful ministry for more than 9 years. Serious health issues took Brian and Mychelle off the field in 2012. Brian worked in the Financial Services industry for five years prior to going to work in the BBFI Mission Office in 2017. This has served him well in his position as Finance Director. Brian is also the Director of the World Initiative Network. Being an adjunct faculty member allows for a strong connection between the BBFI Mission Office, and the students and faculty of Mission U. Brian teaches one seated class each semester within the Intercultural Studies department. He also facilitates two online courses for Mission University. SEAN GRIER Online Degrees Faculty; Criminal Justice & Leadership – 2020 Education: BS, Liberty University, 2007; M.Div., Liberty Theological Seminary, 2010; MS Criminal Justine, University of Cincinnati, 2012; Ph.D. Criminal Justice: Organizational Leadership, Nova Southeastern University, 2018. Favorite Bible Passage: Colossians 2:13-14 Hobbies: Hunting, Fishing, Camping Blog/Wesbite: https://www.linkedin.com/in/sean-grier-phd-92aaa98b/ Bio: Dr. Sean Grier is an adjunct faculty member with Mission University. Dr. Grier has been teaching collegiate level courses in a variety of formats since 2010. Dr. Grier earned his PhD in Criminal Justice from Nova Southeastern University. Additionally, Dr. Grier earned his MS in Criminal Justice from the University of Cincinnati, as well as a MDiv and MA from Liberty Theological Seminary. Dr. Grier completed his undergraduate studies at Liberty University. Dr. Grier’s research interests include biosocial criminology, gun policy issues, and faith-based correctional programming. Dr. Grier has an extensive professional background, including thirty-two years of professional law enforcement experience. Dr. Grier began his career on active duty with the U.S. Army Military Police and later transitioned to a position as a uniformed Police Officer in the Washington, D.C. area. Dr. Grier then accepted a position as a Special Agent with the Defense Security Service, headquartered out of the Pentagon, where he witnessed the horrific attacks on 9/11. Dr. Grier was employed for over 23 years with the Federal Air Marshal Service in a variety of supervisory roles within the Department of Homeland Security. Dr. Grier retired from federal service in May 2025. JON HALEY Online Degrees Faculty – 2020 Education: BS, Mission University, 1995; MA Christian Leadership, Liberty University, 2009. Local Church: Hallmark Church (TX) Favorite Bible Passage: Philippians 2:1-11 Hobbies: Reading, writing, working out, hiking Publications: “Unshakeable Hope: Anchoring Your Soul in God’s Promises” “BEYOND: Going Further Together” “In Him: Behavior Reveals Beliefs” “RISK: Dare to Embrace the Heart of God” “Fight for Your Family: Capturing the Heart of Your Child” “I Must God: An Epic Journey of Knowing God and Finding Purpose” “TRUST: Will You Choose to Trust God Until He Proves It?” “ABIDE: An Abiding Life Leads to an Abundant Life” https://www.amazon.com/stores/Jon-Haley/author/B08FBGJ3MY?ref=ap_rdr&isDramIntegrated=true&shoppingPortalEnabled=true Bio: Jon is a 1993 graduate of Mission University and has been serving as the lead pastor of Hallmark Church in Fort Worth, TX since 2016. He loves Mission U and is thankful for the opportunity to invest in future leaders. CHADD HARKRIDER Registrar; Pastoral & Leadership Faculty – 2022 Education: BS, Mission University, 2005; MAOL, Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2022. Local Church: South Side Baptist (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Colossians 3:17 Hobbies: Anything that allows him to spend time with his wife, family, and friends Professional Affiliations: Delta Epsilon Chi 2005, 2022 Bio: Chadd has been married to his wonderful wife, Morgen, since 1993. Together, they have two daughters, a son-in-law, and a beloved granddaughter. The entire Harkrider family are proud graduates of Mission University, where they now serve in various capacities at MU and the Baptist Bible Fellowship International. Chadd built a distinguished 21-year career in law enforcement, where he served in leadership roles as a patrolman, detective, hostage negotiator, and City Marshal. In 2001, he surrendered to serve in the Gospel ministry, transitioning into pastoral leadership. His dedication to both fields has given him a unique perspective on service, commitment, and leadership. Today, Chadd continues to impact lives through his pastoral work while cherishing his family and faith in the Lord Jesus Christ. KENZIE HARKRIDER Online Degrees Faculty; Ministry – 2021 Education: BS, Mission University, 2020; MACM, Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2022. Local Church: South Side Baptist (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Psalm 65:5 Hobbies: Spending time with family and friends, biking, taking walks, spending time outside when the weather is nice, shopping, organizing, and traveling about the U.S. and Europe Professional Affiliations: Delta Epsilon Chi (2020) Bio: Kenzie has served in the online programs at Mission University since the spring of 2021. She is a two-time Mission University graduate with her Bachelors in Business Managment and her Masters in Church Ministry and is the recipient of multiple academic awards and honors. Kenzie has a background in customer service, retail and business development, and social media management. She is a member of South Side Baptist Church in Springfield and serves faithfully as the Director of Children’s Ministry. NATHANIEL HARMON Music Faculty – 2010 Education: BA, Mission University, 1999; MACM Worship, Liberty Baptist Theological Seminary, 2016. RANDY HARP Ministry Faculty – 2011 Education: BA, Mission University, 1999; MAR Leadership, Liberty Baptist Theological Seminary, 2008; M.Div. Leadership, Liberty Baptist Theological Seminary, 2009; D.Min. Pastoral Leadership, Southwestern Baptist Theological Seminary, 2022 Local Church: High Street (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: John 3:30 Hobbies: Anything with family, all things Arkansas Razorbacks, golf, reading, traveling. Website: www.tribune.org, www.randyharp.net Publications: “Searching for Wisdom: 31 Day Devotional Through Proverbs,” “The Revitalization of a Network of Churches,” Baptist Bible Tribune articles Professional Affiliations: Evangelical Theological Society, Baptist Bible Fellowship International Bio: Randy Harp serves as the Executive Director of the Baptist Bible Fellowship Central Office, Publisher at Tribune Publishers, and Editor-in-Chief of the Baptist Bible Tribune. In these leadership roles, he collaborates closely with Christian leaders across the globe, a rich experience that has shaped the insights shared in his writings and teaching. He holds a Doctor of Ministry from Southwestern Baptist Theological Seminary, a Master of Divinity and a Master of Arts in Leadership from Liberty University, and a bachelor’s degree in Pastoral Ministry from Mission University. Randy’s ministry experience outside of the BBFI Central Office includes serving as senior pastor for two churches, one of which he founded, along with his time as a division chair and faculty member at Baptist Bible College. Randy resides in Springfield, MO, with his wife, Stacy, and they are blessed with four children. CHARLES HODGES, JR Biblical Counseling Faculty – 2012 Education: BA, Indiana University, 1972; MD, Indiana University School of Medicine, 1975; MA, Liberty University, 1989; MAR Counseling, Liberty University, 2002; Certified Biblical Counselor, ACBC; Fellow, ACBC. SCOTT HUDGINS Missions/Intercultural Studies Faculty – 2018 Education: BA, Mission University, 1998; MA Muslim Studies, Columbia International University, 2004; D.Min. Missions, Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary, ABD. CHANEIKA JACKSON Online Degrees Faculty; Organizational Leadership – 2023 Education: AA, Mission University, 2011; BS, Mission University, 2011; MAOL, Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2022. Local Church: Grace Church (AR) Favorite Bible Passage: 2 Peter 3:9-15; Matthew 20:26-28; Colossians 3:23 Hobbies: Any and all sports, board games, traveling Bio: Chaneika serves as the Communications Director and is a member of the Young Adult Leadership team at her church. She is dedicated to empowering individuals and fostering personal growth. She currently facilitates leadership courses at Mission U Online, equipping students with the skills to overcome challenges and encouraging them to make meaningful contributions to their positions in ministry and their community. In her roles, Chaneika develops communication strategies and nurtures leadership skills among young adults. She is passionate about creating an environment where young adults can thrive both personally and spiritually. Her approach combines practical skills with an understanding of individual needs, supporting students as they navigate their unique journeys. Serving in the church is a cornerstone of her life and work. She finds great joy in witnessing the growth of those she works with, especially as they discover their potential and deepen their faith. She says it is incredibly rewarding to see her students (and those she gets to serve in her church) step into their strengths and embrace new opportunities. She is inspired by the progress and success of the young adults she has had the privilege to work with. Together, we are building a community of strong, capable leaders ready to make a positive impact. KIMBERLY JANSON Education Faculty – 2018 Education: BS, Mission University, 2010; M.Ed. Curriculum & Instruction, Evangel University, 2015; TESOL Certification, 2015. JON JONES Director of Academic and Library Services; Education Faculty – 2006 Education: BS, Mission University, 2000; MLIS, Valdosta State University, 2014; Ed.D. Leadership, Union University, ABD. Local Church: First Baptist, Willard (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Philippians 4:4-8 Hobbies: In my free time, I love spending quality moments with my family and enjoying suspense thriller movies, as well as following shows like The Voice and NBC’s Chicago series. I’m an avid sports enthusiast, supporting all Dallas-area teams and passionately cheering for Texas A&M University. Music is a constant companion in my day, with Spotify often playing in my office. Additionally, I have a deep interest in leadership and enjoy expanding my knowledge through a growing collection of books on the subject. Publications: Andrews, Grace.; Carey, Renee D.; Jones, Jon; Mancuso, J. James; and McConkey, Deborah H. (2022) “Distributed collection development: How to grow your library without knowing everything” The Christian Librarian. Available at: https://digitalcommons.georgefox.edu/tcl/vol65/iss1/12 Jones, J. (2022). Tell your story. In The Association of Christian Librarians, Faithful Words: A collection of Reference Point Devotions for Librarians. The Association of Christian Librarians. Also available at: http://www.acl.org/index.cfm/spiritual-encouragement/devotional-archives/ Carey, Renee D.; Jones, Jon; Ladwig, Laura M.; Mancuso, J. James; and McConkey, Deborah H. (2020) “Flying solo” The Christian Librarian: Vol. 63 : Iss. 1 , Article 5. Available at: https://digitalcommons.georgefox.edu/tcl/vol63/iss1/5 Jones, J. (2017). “Anderson’s “Lost island smugglers” and “Captain Jack’s treasure” (Book Review),” The Christian Librarian: Vol. 60 : Iss. 2 , Article 73. Available at: https://digitalcommons.georgefox.edu/tcl/vol60/iss2/73 Jones, J. (2017). “Wellum’s “Christ alone – the uniqueness of Jesus as savior” (Book Review),” The Christian Librarian: Vol. 60 : Iss. 2 , Article 22. Available at: https://digitalcommons.georgefox.edu/tcl/vol60/iss2/22 Professional Affiliations: Commissioner, Association for Biblical Higher Education Commission on Accreditation. (2018 – Present). Team Evaluator, Association for Biblical Higher Education Commission on Accreditation. (2019 – Present). Secretary, Association for Biblical Higher Education Commission on Accreditation. (2024 – Present). Association of Christian Librarians. (2009 – Present). Christian Library Consortium. (2010-2012, 2020 – Present). Library and Information Resource Network (2020 – Present). Missouri Professors of Educational Administration (2024 – Present). ABHE Liaison, Bible Core Section, Association of Christian Librarians, 2024 – Present. Bio: Jon serves as the Director of Library & Academic Services at Mission University, where he has worked in various capacities since 2006. He is pursuing an Ed.D. in Higher Education at Union University, building on his degrees in Library Science and Pastoral studies. Jon has experience in academic leadership, teaching, and research, with expertise in educational research, library science, and educational leadership. He currently teaches courses like College Study Skills, Action Research, and Children’s Literature. Additionally, Jon is active in accreditation through his work with the Association for Biblical Higher Education and has presented at numerous professional conferences. Beyond his professional life, Jon and his wife Beth, who have been married since 1995, are proud parents of four children and grandparents to three. They reside in Willard, Missouri, where Jon has served as an alderman and held ministry roles in two different churches, focusing on administration, music, and youth leadership. He is an avid advocate for maximizing library resources in education and is a published author in library science and Christian education. CRYSTAL KEMPER Education Faculty – 2024 Education: BS, Mission University, 2003; M.Ed. Counseling Development – School Counseling, Lamar University, 2023. Local Church: Granbury Baptist (TX) Favorite Bible Passage: Proverbs 3:5-6 Hobbies: Being a home barista and creating new recipes for lattes Professional Affiliations: American School Counselor Association (ASCA) Bio: Crystal has been married to her husband, Brian, for 22 years. They have four children: Anna, Jude, Whitman, and Reese. Crystal is a 2003 graduate of Mission University and a 2023 graduate of Lamar University with her master’s degree. She has been teaching in Texas public schools for over 17 years and has spent the last 3 years interning in the school counseling department. She is excited to be teaching as an adjunct faculty member at Mission University in the Education department. BENJAMIN LAIRD Online Degrees Faculty; New Testament – 2021 Education: BS, Liberty University, 2003; M.Div., Southern Baptist Theological Seminary, 2006; Th.M., Southern Baptist Theological Seminary, 2009; M.Litt., University of St. Andrews, 2010; Ph.D. Divinity, University of Aberdeen, 2016. Mark Larson History & Education Faculty – 2025 Education: Doctor of Education, Liberty University, 2024 Specialist of Education, Liberty University, 2009 Master of Education – Teaching, The University of Texas at Arlington, 2007 Bachelor of Science, Southwestern Assemblies of God University, 2002 Local Church: North Point Church (Springfield, MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Ephesians 2:10 Hobbies: I enjoy coaching, traveling, and attending my boys’ activities. My wife and I are Kansas City Royals fans and spend as many summer evenings as possible at the K. Bio: My wife Shari and I have been married for 25 years, and we have three boys: Hayden, Jayce, and Kyler. I started teaching and coaching in 2002 after graduating from Southwestern Assemblies of God University in Waxahachie, Texas, where I played football for the Lions. I completed my M.Ed. at the University of Texas at Arlington in 2007 and then my Ed.S. at Liberty University in 2009. In 2022, I returned to Liberty to complete my Ed.D. and finished it in the fall of 2024. I currently teach and coach at Kickapoo High School and joined the Mission University team as an adjunct faculty member in the spring of 2025. DAVID LILES Online Degrees Faculty; Leadership – 2021 Education: BA, Mission University, 1987; M.Div., Grace Theological Seminary, 1989; M.Div. Counseling, Liberty Baptist Theological Seminary, 1991; D.Min. Leadership, Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary, 2010; Th.M., Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary, 2019; Ph.D. Biblical Studies: Biblical Ministry, Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary, 2019. RUTH MADEWELL Chair of General Studies; English Faculty – 2022 Education: BA, Pacific Coast Baptist Bible College, 1992; M.Ed. Teaching & Learning, Maranatha Baptist University, 2020; Graduate Certificate in English, Maranatha Baptist University, 2023. Local Church: Baptist Temple (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Psalm 37:4 Hobbies: Reading, shopping at flea markets, collecting antique Mason jars Professional Affiliations: National Council of Teachers of English (NCTE) Bio: Ruth has a passion for teaching English, along with a love for reading and writing. She has been happily married to her husband John for over 31 years, and together they have been blessed with a wonderful family – their son, daughter, son-in-law, and two beautiful grandchildren . Before joining MU, Ruth had the privilege of teaching English at the high school level where she built a strong foundation in helping students grow both academically and personally. She holds a certification in Teaching with AI and is interested in how AI can be used in the classroom to enhance learning while maintaining academic integrity. Her heart is fully committed to her students’ academic success and spiritual growth, and she truly cherishes the opportunity to build meaningful connections with each of them. Ruth’s ultimate goal as a teacher is to help students develop strong writing skills that will serve them in their careers and their service to the Lord. JOSHUA MATHEWS Biblical Counseling Faculty – 2018 Education: BA, Mission University, 2001; M.Div., Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2007; Certified Biblical Counselor, ACBC. Local Church: Meadowview Baptist (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Philippians 2:1-10 Hobbies: Exercise (ex-runner, who is limited to walking these days), reading and watching science fiction, Zelda video game franchise Website: joshualmathews.com Professional Affiliations: ACBC (Association of Certified Biblical Counselors) Bio: Joshua has practiced Biblical counseling in ministry for over 25 years. He had the privilege of learning from and working with some of the finest teachers in the field including Dr. Kevin Carson and Bill Piatt, fellow faculty members at Mission University. He is married to Faith and is the father of Alethea, Amos, Caedmon, and Judson. JAN MCCLELLAN Education Faculty – 2025 Education: BSC, Evangel University, 2010; M.Ed., Southwest Baptist University, 2014. Local Church: Crossway Baptist (MO) Professional Affiliations: MIDTESOL. DANA MEINDERS Women’s Softball Coach; Education Faculty – 2023 Education: BS, Missouri Southern State University, 1993; M.Ed., Southwest Baptist University, 1996. Favorite Bible Passage: 1 John 4:4 Hobbies: Traveling and reading Bio: Dana has dedicated 27 years to the field of public education where she had the privilege of inspiring and shaping the lives of countless students. Her journey as an educator has been both fulfilling and transformative, allowing her to connect with young minds and foster a love for learning. On a personal note, she is the proud wife of Darin Meinders, with whom she has shared 30 wonderful years. Together they have built a loving family that includes two sons, Dallas and Dawson. Family means everything to them, and she cherishes the memories they have created together over the years. Dallas is married to Mia, who has brought an additional layer of joy to their family. Dana is thrilled to be a grandmother to their beautiful granddaughter, Charli, who lights up their lives with her presence. As she reflects on her journey, Dana is grateful for the opportunity to continue doing what she loves – educate, coach, and nurture her relationship with God. She is very proud to be a part of the Mission University family and will continue to embrace her commitment to God, family education and personal growth. DARIN MEINDERS Athletic Director; Golf Coach – 2019 Education: BS, Central Missouri State University, 1991; M.Ed. Administration: Secondary Administration, William Woods University, 2000. BARB MILIONI Leadership & Ministry Faculty – 2022 Education: BS, Mission University, 1988; MAOL, Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2021. Local Church: First Baptist Willard (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Hebrews 12:1-2 Hobbies: Reading, gardening, traveling with her husband Website: compelled.life Publications: “What Pastor’s Wives Wish Their Husbands Knew About Them.” Focus on the Family, March 1999. “How to Really Appreciate Your Pastor.” Baptist Bible Tribune. October 2017. “Thankful for the Scars.” Baptist Bible Tribune. November 2018. Bio: Barb Milioni has worked alongside her husband, Mission University President Mark Milioni, for the past 40 years. Together, they have led growing ministries through church revitalization, building projects, church planting, Christian education, and higher education. Barb has effectively developed and led children’s and preschool ministries, instilling a passion for Jesus and for learning in young hearts and minds. Barb loves teaching and enjoys leading Bible studies for women and speaking at women’s events. Her love for teaching is fueled by her love for learning. Barb’s greatest passions are spending time with her husband, whether at work or at their home, and their ten grandchildren (made possible by her four wonderful children and their spouses). MARK MILIONI President of Mission University; Chair of Ministry Studies; Ministry & Leadership Faculty – 2012 Education: BS, Mission University, 1988; MA Pastoral Ministry, Luther Rice Seminary; PhD, Louisiana Baptist University; Ph.D. Organizational Leadership, Regent University, 2023. Bio: Mark Milioni has served as the president of Mission University since May, 2012. His leadership has resulted in a tremendous financial turn-around, numerical growth, and a renewed spirit and passion for training men and women for the ministry at the college. Dr. Milioni graduated from Mission University in 1988 with a bachelor’s degree in Pastoral Ministry. He continued his education at Luther Rice Seminary, earning a master’s degree in ministry; at Louisiana Baptist University, earning a Doctorate in Communications, and at Regent University, earning a Doctorate in Organizational Leadership. He has served the Lord in the local church as a senior pastor for over twenty-five years, giving him a great love for the church and for pastors. His education and experience uniquely qualify him to lead the college as it endeavors to create a life changing experience for men and women who will go forth to change the world for Jesus Christ. STEVEN MOWRIS Math Professor – 2007 Education: BS, Mission University, 1977; M. Ed. Reading, Missouri State University, 1988. Local Church: Hillside Baptist Church (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: 1 Corinthians 10:13 Hobbies: Hunting, fishing, camping, sports, and sometimes table games Bio: After graduating from high school, Steven joined the United States Air Force. There he met the girl who would become his wife. His fourth and final year was spent in a remote tour of duty in South Korea, and it was there that a missionary in Seoul told him about Mission University. During the summer of his junior year, the Lord burdened him about being an elementary teacher which caused him to switch degree paths. After graduation, he taught for 30 years, reared 4 children (with the help of an awesome wife) and came full circle by becoming part of the faculty dedicated to investing in the lives of those who desire to be school teachers. SHANNON MULFORD Academic Dean; Director of Institutional Research; Ministry Faculty – 2017 Education: BA, Mission University, 2017; MACM, Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2019; D.Ed.Min., Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary (ABD). Local Church: Park Crest Baptist Church (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Romans 5:8-9 Hobbies: Traveling with his wife and family, exploring national and state parks, visiting historical locations, antiquing, fishing, and golf Professional Affiliations: Association for Biblical Higher Education (ABHE); Council for Adult and Experiential Learning (CAEL); Delta Epsilon Chi Bio: Shannon is married to the love of his life, Tonya, since 1993, and they have three grown children and a grandchild. Shannon graduated from Mission University with a Bachelor of Arts degree in Pastoral Studies and graduated from Baptist Bible Theological Seminary with a Master of Arts degree in Church Ministry. He is currently in the dissertation stages of the Doctor of Educational Ministry (D.Ed.Min.) program at Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary. He has served the Lord in the local church for over 20 years. He also worked more than 16 years in the insurance and finance industry, holding both managerial and professional positions within operations at FCCI Insurance Group as well as a position as a licensed financial advisor and insurance agent with Purpose Financial Group/LPL. Shannon has been recognized with multiple business service and academic awards. BENJAMIN NEWHOUSE Business Law Faculty – 2022 Education: BS, University of Tulsa, 1996; JD, University of Tulsa – College of Law, 2000. Published Articles: The Missouri Bar (April 2026) Oklahoma Bar Association (May 2026) JEFF PAYNE Music Faculty – 2023 Education: BM, University of Arkansas, 2014; M.Ed. Music, Missouri State University, in progress. Local Church: The Courageous Church (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Psalm 27:14 Hobbies: Playing Pokemon Go with his son, creating music, going on short hikes Professional Affiliations: Missouri Music Educators Association (MMEA) Bio: Jeff has served as the Associate Director of Band and Choir at Kickapoo High School since 2021. He previously worked as the assistant band director and guitar instructor in the Hollister R-V School District. Jeff also serves as the volunteer Worship Director at The Courageous Church, North Campus, in Springfield, MO. DIANNA PARKER Business & Leadership Faculty – 2021 Education: Certificate in Accounting and Data Processing, Truman State University; BS, Drury University, 1986; MBA, Missouri State University, 1989; Graduate Certificate in Institutional Research, University of Missouri-St. Louis, 2005; Ph.D. Educational Leadership, University of St. Louis-Missouri, 2011. BILL PIATT Biblical Counseling Faculty – 2005 Education: BS, Mission University, 2004; Fellow, Association of Certified Biblical Counselors, 2006; M.Div., Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2009. Local Church: Sonrise Baptist (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: 2 Corinthians 5:9 Professional Affiliations: Association of Certified Biblical Counselors (ACBC), International Association of Biblical Counselors (IABC) Bio: Bill has 50 years of experience in Biblical Counseling and along with his being adjunct faculty for the University, he is an Association of Certified Biblical Counselors (ACBC) Fellow. His experience adds real world applications to the subjects taught. SHARON PRICE Online Degrees Faculty; Business & Finance – 2024 Education: BS, Evangel University, 1991; MSM, Indiana Wesleyan University, 2005; DBA Accounting, Anderson University, 2014; CPA. DEVIN PRITCHARD Teaching Assistant for Music Faculty – 2024 Education: BS, Southwest Baptist University, 2008; BM, Southwest Baptist University, 2008; M.Div., Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary, 2017. Local Church: Harmony Baptist (MO) Favorite Bible Passage: Colossians 3:23 Hobbies: Hiking, fishing, going to the movies, football & pretty much any sport or outdoor activity. Professional Affiliations: Southern Baptist Convention Church Music Conference Bio: Devin currently serves as the Worship & Discipleship pastor at Harmony Baptist Church in Rogersville, Missouri. He felt the Lord’s leading to also serve in the University setting helping to train the next generation of men and women to lead the Lord’s church in worship and ministry. He is married to his wife, Traci, who is a Vocal Music professor. They have been married for 15 years and have two sons, Henry & Jonathan, who attend the Logan-Rogersville School District. MARCIA RAINS Online Degrees Faculty; Education – 2024 Education: BA, Mission University, 1983; BS, St. Mary of the Plains College, 1992; M.Ed. Gifted Education, Ft. Hays State University, 1994; Ed.D. School Administration, Oklahoma State University, 2015. Local Church: Heritage Baptist Church (OK) Favorite Bible Passage: Psalm 139:14 Hobbies: Crocheting, riding a bicycle or seeing the U.S. from the back of a Harley Bio: Dr. Rains holds a 31-year teaching career in public education. Before retiring, she spent 29 of those years working with academically gifted students from kindergarten through high school. During that time, she completed her master’s degree in special education, earned the National Board Certification, and completed her Doctorate degree in Educational Leadership. Her desire as an instructor for MU is to help prepare the next generation of education leaders to meet the challenges of today’s educational environment. Dr. Rains and her husband have two married children and four grandchildren. Wesley Scroggins Business Faculty – 2025 Education: PhD, Management, New Mexico State University, 2003 MS, Industrial/Organizational Psychology, Missouri State University, 1997 MDiv, Biblical Studies, Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary, 1990 BA, Religious Studies, Southwest Baptist University, 1987 BA, Psychology, Southwest Baptist University, 1987 Bio: Dr. Wesley Scroggins is a Professor of Management at Missouri State University. He teaches courses in human resource management and organizational behavior. He received his Ph.D. in management from New Mexico State University and holds an M.S. degree in industrial-organizational psychology from Missouri State University. Dr. Scroggins also holds an MDiv. degree from Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary and is an ordained minister. Dr. Scroggins is the Executive Director of Abolish Abortion Missouri. He is active in the fight to end abortion in Missouri and works with state legislators on abortion abolition legislation. He also works to educate the church on the issues impacting the culture. He resides in Billings, MO where he operates a small farm. DONALD SEWELL Online Degrees Faculty; Business & Economics – 2021 Education: BS, Midwestern State University, 2001; MBA, Strayer University, 2009; DBA, Walden University, 2022. JON SLAYDEN Online Degrees Faculty; Ministry – 2020 Education: BS, Mission University, 1999; MACM, Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2016. Wayne Slusser New Testament & Biblical Languages Faculty – 2001-2015; 2025 Education: Ph.D. in New Testament/Greek, Baptist Bible Seminary, Clarks Summit, PA, 2012 M.Div. Baptist Bible Graduate School, Springfield, MO, 2001 Master of Arts in Biblical Studies, Baptist Bible Graduate School, Springfield, MO, 2000 Bachelor of Science in Environmental Design, University of Oklahoma, Norman, OK, 1991 Local Church: Bible Baptist Church, Buffalo, MO (Pastor) Favorite Bible Passage: Mark 10:45 Hobbies: Spending time with his wife, playing sports, and landscaping Blog/Website: www.ntresources.com Bio: Dr. Slusser was born and reared in Northeast Ohio. He received a degree in Landscape Architecture from the University of Oklahoma (1991). While working in Ohio, he met his wife, Melissa, and they were married in 1993. It was in 1996 that God ordered Wayne’s steps to attend Seminary, and he surrendered to full-time ministry. He graduated with his M.Div. in 2001 and was asked to be on faculty at Baptist Bible College & Theological Seminary, Springfield, MO for 14 years (2001-2015). He also received his PhD in New Testament & Greek (2012) and was the co-pastor (2001-2015) of a team church plant, Sonrise Baptist Church (Ozark, MO). God moved Wayne and his family to Baptist Bible Seminary, Clarks Summit University to teach, coach soccer, and assume the role of Seminary Dean (2015-2024). Since September of 2024, Dr. Slusser has been pastoring Bible Baptist Church (Buffalo, MO) with solid teaching from God’s Word, a heart for the growth of the church, and a desire for the church’s walk to be worthy of the gospel. Dr. Slusser and his wife, Melissa, have two sons (Jack and Nick). Publications: Books/book chapters published as author, co-author, or editor: A Daily Greek Devotional: 365 Devotions on the Greek New Testament, contributor of 10 devotions. Bennington, VT. Northeastern Baptist Press, 2023. Death and Discipleship: An Analysis of the Predictions of Jesus’ Death in the Gospel of Mark. Academic Theological Studies, Vol. 3. Bennington, VT. Northeastern Baptist Press, 2023. Scripture’s Story: A Unifying Hope. Bennington, VT. Northeastern Baptist Press. 2021, (co-author). “The Structural Analysis of Philemon.” M.Div. Thesis. Theological Research Exchange Network (TREN), 2001. Journals (peer-reviewed): “The Pastor’s Preoccupation: To lead? Or to follow?” The Baptist Bulletin, May/June 2019: 15-18. “(Re)Defining the Gospels: Mark as a Test Case, Part Two.” The Journal of Ministry & Theology, vol. 23:2 (fall 2019): 124-153. “Jesus Stills the Storm (Mark 4:35-41).” The Journal of Ministry & Theology, vol. 22:2 (fall 2018): 18-45. “Imprisoned for the Glory of God: Considering Ryrie’s Third Aspect of the Sine Qua Non of Dispensationalism.” The Journal of Ministry & Theology, vol. 22:1 (Spring 2018): 146-68. “(Re)Defining the Gospels: Mark as A Test Case, Part One.” The Journal of Ministry & Theology, vol. 21:2 (fall 2017): 42-76. “Jonah’s Rescue: What Are the Implications for Today (Jonah 1:17-2:10).” The Journal of Ministry & Theology, vol. 21:1 (spring 2017): 5-41. “Implications for Pastoral Ministry Based on Paul’s Prayer in 1 Thessalonians 3:9-13.” The Journal of Ministry & Theology, vol. 20:1 (spring 2016): 123-51. “The Role of Women in Ministry.” Baptist Preacher’s Journal 16, no 2 (Winter 2006): 20-26. 2006. Articles (magazine, website, blog, etc.): Spectrum Study Bible (iPhone app) – Expert Advisory Board Member and New Testament Commentary ‘nugget’ Authoring Team (creator and contributor to the development of a Bible app for study and reading) (2015 – Present) Personal blog/website ( https://ntresources.com ) (2015 – Present) Greek for a Week (weekly Greek video series) (2018 – Present) “The Bible God Intended?” Baptist Bible Tribune 57, no 11 (July/Aug): 8-11, 2007. ZACHARY STEWART Dean of Students; Ministry Faculty – 2024 Education: BS, Mission University, 2019; MACM, Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2021; M.Div., Mission University, 2024. JASON TODD VP of Finance; Business Faculty – 2021 Education: BS, Mission University, 1994; MA, Louisiana Baptist University, 2000; MAOL, Baptist Bible Theological Seminary, 2021. ROXANE TRIPLETT Education Faculty – 2023 Education: BS, Midwestern State University, 1988; M.Ed. Elementary Education, Missouri State University, 2001. TODD WITTE Online Degrees Faculty; Leadership – 2020 Education: BS, Boston Baptist College, 1995; MA Management & Leadership, Liberty University, 2016. Local Church: Midway Church (TX) Favorite Bible Passage: Acts 13:1-3 Hobbies: SCUBA diving, camping off the grid, fly fishing, traveling with his wife and exploring local restaurants and dishes that help them connect to the culture Bio: Todd is a passionate follower of Jesus Christ who has been in ministry for over 25 years. As a leader of leaders, he loves the “aha” moment when ministry leaders and teams see their potential and embrace their God inspired vision for the future. Ministry leaders often need reinforcement of their God-given passion for people and great teaching and preaching gifts. He has a passion for equipping ministry leaders to be great leaders for the ministries they serve. He coaches church planters and ministry leaders, is involved with church planter assessments, provides professional ministry consultation, and actively serves in his local church. Mr. Witte currently serves as the Executive Director of the international missions service agency, One Another Ministries. He loves the opportunity to care for those who care for the world by leading this great ministry. Married in 1991, Todd and Amy have three grown children and a grandson: Katie and Matt Morton (2020 graduates of Mission University), Kim and Jordan Bailey, and Nicklas. They reside in Pilot Point, TX where they are active members of Midway Church. WALT WITHAM Online Degrees Faculty; Business & Finance – 2025 Education: BBA, Northcentral University, 2008; MSCJ, University of Cincinnati, 2009; Ph.D. Financial Management with Criminal Justice Concentration, Northcentral University, 2018 . Local Church: Northstar (OH) Favorite Bible Passage: 2 Peter 1:3 Hobbies: Amateur radio and bowling Professional Affiliations : Financial Management Association International (FMA) and Academy of Criminal Justice Science (ACJS). Publications: “Constipated Curricula vs. Cross Fertilization: How Universities Can Breed Entrepreneurial Leaders,” Pardo, N., Witham, W., Gordon, B., Gillies, B., Kettemborough, C., Morris, M., Hoon, S. “An Exploration of Police Officer Perceptions of Information Sharing Effectiveness,” Scholars Press, Beau Bassin, Mauritius. Bio: Dr. Witham facilitates in Mission University’s MBA program online. Due to the dual specialization nature of his Ph.D. in both Financial Management and Criminal Justice, his past areas of research interest have both a business and criminal justice flavor, focusing on the effectiveness of knowledge management initiatives in the proliferation of intelligence-led policing at the local level. His future research will most likely be focused on BioSocial Criminology or the impact of witnessing trauma on first responders. He has also conducted broad research on the nature and response of currency markets to geopolitical events. In addition, he serves as Senior Chaplain with the SW Ohio chapter of the International Fellowship of Chaplains, has achieved his Extra class amateur radio operator’s license, and serves in his church’s new church plant serving and discipling in an up-and-coming community. Our Home Town Springfield, Missouri Mission University finds its home in Springfield, Missouri, a charming city full of one-of-a-kind attractions, historical treasures, entertaining sports, and a lively culture right on Route 66. Mission U is less than 4 miles from Downtown where one would find unique coffee shops, restaurants, boutiques, and the Springfield famous, Hurt’s Donuts. While in Springfield, don’t forget to catch a Springfield Cardinals game in Hammon’s Stadium or visit the home of Bass Pro Shops! The locals never take for granted picking up a Jackhammer Concrete from Andy’s Frozen Custard located 2 miles down the road from Mission U or spending time at the Farmer’s markets Saturday mornings before trailing to the nearest seasonal festival. With ample coffee shops, hole-in-the-wall cuisine, and shopping selections there is never a dull moment in the home of Mission University. Student Life Schedule a visit About Beliefs & Values Accreditation Faculty Institutional Learning Outcomes Institutional Research & Effectiveness Hours of Operation Notice of Non-Discriminitory Policy CARES, CRRSA, ARP Funding Information Contact Us Admissions Apply Now Visit Campus Request Information Student Housing Transfer to Mission U Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Contact Admissions Academics On-Campus Degrees Online Degrees Library Transcript Request Diploma Request Meet Faculty Student Life Student Housing Campus Events Catalogs & Handbooks Registrar Financial Services Register for Classes Academic Calendar Campus Security Library Chapel Alumni & Friends Give Book a Team/Speaker Resources Academic Resources Financial Aid Consumer Information News Job Opportunities Campus Mail Dining Services EADA Report Campus Security Professional Licensure Disclosure Follow Follow Follow Follow Mission University 628 E Kearney Street Springfield, Missouri 65803 Student Login"
    },
